--
-- THE PHARMA FIXTURE - Story 1, the clean lot, and Story 2, the problem lot.
-- `fixture_pharma.md` is the narrative.
--
-- STORY 2 IS WHERE THE TWO PARTICIPANTS STOP AGREEING. Every template of
-- Story 1 names parties from both organizations, so both see all of it -
-- which is correct for a joint process and shows no privacy at all.
-- `Quarantine` names NO supplier party: a lot held back is the producer's
-- own decision until it chooses to raise a deviation, and that is the
-- materially different view `fixture_pharma.md` asks the fixture to produce.
--
-- TWO ORGANIZATIONS ON TWO PARTICIPANTS. Every producer party is hosted on
-- app-provider and every supplier party on app-user, which is what LocalNetND
-- presents once the Super Validator is set aside as infrastructure - his
-- correction of 2026-09-21.
--
-- A PARTY PER ACTUAL USER - his instruction, 2026-09-22. The model had one
-- `producer` party and one `supplier` party, which is a label for an
-- organization and not a party anybody in one would hold. Each organization
-- now carries the roles `fixture_pharma.md` names in its Topology section -
-- Procurement, Quality Assurance, Receiving and Manufacturing on the producer;
-- Sales, Production, Quality Assurance and Shipping on the supplier - and each
-- is one real person with one ledger user behind it. A choice is controlled by
-- the role that would sign for it in the plant, not by the company.
--
-- WHICH MEANS OBSERVERS ARE NOW LOAD BEARING. A controller that is not a
-- stakeholder cannot see the contract it is meant to act on, so every template
-- names the roles that must read it next. That is not decoration: it is the
-- privacy statement of the fixture, and it is what makes `sv` and the other
-- organization's roles NOT see what they should not.
--
-- EVERY CHOICE IS STILL CONTROLLED FROM ONE PARTICIPANT AT A TIME. A
-- submission carries the authority of the parties acting in it plus the
-- authority the exercised contract delegates, so the propose/accept chain
-- commits from a single participant and never needs a party hosted on both.
-- MEASURED 2026-09-22, `probes/pharma`: the producer's authority reaches the
-- supplier's participant through the choice, and the reverse exercise is
-- refused with DAML_AUTHORIZATION_ERROR. Splitting the parties by role does not
-- move that line - `AcceptOrder` is still exercised by a supplier-side party
-- against a contract a producer-side party signed.
--
-- RICH TYPES SINCE 2026-09-22, and every one of them measured before it was
-- used: an enum on the disposition, a variant on the supplier's response and
-- a map on the retest - `probes/pharma/types_probe.py`, which submitted each
-- candidate encoding against a running participant and recorded what was
-- refused as well as what was taken.
--
-- KEYLESS - his decision, 2026-09-22, the shape D-760 gave Aviation. The stable
-- identifiers are here as Text and a `Pharma Keys` extension is where a key
-- belongs if one is ever wanted.
--
-- Author Claude/bentzn
module Main where

import DA.TextMap (TextMap)

-- | A measured range, as a record inside a record inside a list - the shape
-- `caql_where_design.md` section 4 reaches with a dotted path.
data Range = Range
  with
    low : Decimal
    high : Decimal
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- | HOW STORY 2 ENDS, as an ENUM rather than as Text.
--
-- MEASURED 2026-09-22, `probes/pharma/types_probe.py`: the JSON Ledger API
-- takes an enum as the BARE CONSTRUCTOR STRING - `"ConditionallyAccepted"` -
-- and refuses a tagged object with `Expected ujson.Str`. It was Text carrying
-- one of these five names until that was known, which is what the probe
-- existed to settle.
--
-- THE FIVE ARE `fixture_pharma.md`'s, in its order.
data DispositionOutcome
  = AcceptedAfterInvestigation
  | ConditionallyAccepted
  | RejectedAndReturned
  | Destroyed
  | ReplacedByAnotherLot
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- | What the supplier answered a deviation WITH - a variant, because it is one
-- of these and not several.
--
-- MEASURED the same day: a variant goes as `{"tag": ..., "value": ...}`, and
-- the participant says so itself when it is not - `Variant type json must have
-- 'tag' and 'value' fields`. A constructor taking nothing carries
-- `"value": {}`.
--
-- `fixture_pharma.md`: "The supplier can respond with evidence, additional
-- measurements, explanations, or a proposed corrective action." One response,
-- one of those.
data ResponseEvidence
  = RetainSample QualityTest
  | Statement Text
  | CorrectiveAction Text
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- | One test the supplier or the producer performed.
data QualityTest = QualityTest
  with
    name : Text
    method : Text
    measured : Decimal
    unit : Text
    permitted : Range
    passed : Bool
  deriving (Eq, Show)

-- | What the two organizations agreed the material has to be.
--
-- QUALITY ASSURANCE OWNS A SPECIFICATION on both sides; Procurement reads it
-- because it is what an order is placed against.
template MaterialSpecification
  with
    producerQa : Party
    producerProcurement : Party
    supplierQa : Party
    materialId : Text
    description : Text
    tests : [Text]
  where
    signatory producerQa
    observer producerProcurement, supplierQa

-- | Procurement's proposal. Sales sees it and accepts from its own side;
-- Production sees it because it is what it will be asked to make.
template PurchaseOrder
  with
    producerProcurement : Party
    producerQa : Party
    supplierSales : Party
    supplierProduction : Party
    orderNumber : Text
    materialId : Text
    quantity : Int
    unit : Text
    requiredBy : Date
  where
    signatory producerProcurement
    observer producerQa, supplierSales, supplierProduction

    choice AcceptOrder : ContractId SupplierAcceptance
      with
        acceptedAt : Time
      controller supplierSales
      do
        create SupplierAcceptance with
          producerProcurement = producerProcurement
          producerQa = producerQa
          supplierSales = supplierSales
          supplierProduction = supplierProduction
          orderNumber = orderNumber
          materialId = materialId
          quantity = quantity
          unit = unit
          acceptedAt = acceptedAt

-- | Signed by Procurement AND Sales, which is the contract the whole fixture
-- turns on: two people in two organizations on two participants.
template SupplierAcceptance
  with
    producerProcurement : Party
    producerQa : Party
    supplierSales : Party
    supplierProduction : Party
    orderNumber : Text
    materialId : Text
    quantity : Int
    unit : Text
    acceptedAt : Time
  where
    signatory producerProcurement, supplierSales
    observer producerQa, supplierProduction

    nonconsuming choice RecordLot : ContractId ProductionLot
      with
        lotNumber : Text
        manufacturedOn : Date
        expiresOn : Date
        supplierQa : Party
        supplierShipping : Party
        producerReceiving : Party
      controller supplierProduction
      do
        create ProductionLot with
          supplierProduction = supplierProduction
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          supplierShipping = supplierShipping
          producerQa = producerQa
          producerReceiving = producerReceiving
          orderNumber = orderNumber
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          materialId = materialId
          quantity = quantity
          unit = unit
          manufacturedOn = manufacturedOn
          expiresOn = expiresOn

-- | What Production made. The producer's side watches it and cannot change it.
template ProductionLot
  with
    supplierProduction : Party
    supplierQa : Party
    supplierShipping : Party
    producerQa : Party
    producerReceiving : Party
    orderNumber : Text
    lotNumber : Text
    materialId : Text
    quantity : Int
    unit : Text
    manufacturedOn : Date
    expiresOn : Date
  where
    signatory supplierProduction
    observer supplierQa, supplierShipping, producerQa, producerReceiving

    nonconsuming choice IssueCoa : ContractId CertificateOfAnalysis
      with
        certificateNumber : Text
        issuedAt : Time
        tests : [QualityTest]
      controller supplierQa
      do
        create CertificateOfAnalysis with
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          supplierShipping = supplierShipping
          producerQa = producerQa
          producerReceiving = producerReceiving
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          certificateNumber = certificateNumber
          issuedAt = issuedAt
          tests = tests

-- | The supplier's quality assertion about the lot, signed by the person who
-- made it. Never consumed: it is a fact.
template CertificateOfAnalysis
  with
    supplierQa : Party
    supplierShipping : Party
    producerQa : Party
    producerReceiving : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    certificateNumber : Text
    issuedAt : Time
    tests : [QualityTest]
  where
    signatory supplierQa
    observer supplierShipping, producerQa, producerReceiving

    nonconsuming choice Ship : ContractId Shipment
      with
        shipmentNumber : Text
        shippedAt : Time
        carrier : Text
      controller supplierShipping
      do
        create Shipment with
          supplierShipping = supplierShipping
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          producerQa = producerQa
          producerReceiving = producerReceiving
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          certificateNumber = certificateNumber
          shipmentNumber = shipmentNumber
          shippedAt = shippedAt
          carrier = carrier

-- | In transit. CONSUMED on receipt, so the current state moves with the
-- material and a trail is left behind it.
template Shipment
  with
    supplierShipping : Party
    supplierQa : Party
    producerQa : Party
    producerReceiving : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    certificateNumber : Text
    shipmentNumber : Text
    shippedAt : Time
    carrier : Text
  where
    signatory supplierShipping
    observer supplierQa, producerQa, producerReceiving

    choice Receive : ContractId MaterialReceipt
      with
        receivedAt : Time
        sealIntact : Bool
      controller producerReceiving
      do
        create MaterialReceipt with
          producerReceiving = producerReceiving
          producerQa = producerQa
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          shipmentNumber = shipmentNumber
          receivedAt = receivedAt
          sealIntact = sealIntact

-- | Receiving's own assertion about what arrived. `receivedBy` is gone: the
-- person who received it is the SIGNATORY now, which is the point of a party
-- per actual user - it was a Text field saying what the ledger can prove.
template MaterialReceipt
  with
    producerReceiving : Party
    producerQa : Party
    supplierQa : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    shipmentNumber : Text
    receivedAt : Time
    sealIntact : Bool
  where
    signatory producerReceiving
    observer producerQa, supplierQa

    nonconsuming choice Inspect : ContractId IncomingInspection
      with
        inspectionNumber : Text
        inspectedAt : Time
        tests : [QualityTest]
        conforms : Bool
        remark : Optional Text
        producerManufacturing : Party
      controller producerQa
      do
        create IncomingInspection with
          producerQa = producerQa
          producerReceiving = producerReceiving
          producerManufacturing = producerManufacturing
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          inspectionNumber = inspectionNumber
          inspectedAt = inspectedAt
          tests = tests
          conforms = conforms
          remark = remark

-- | Quality Assurance's independent results, beside the supplier's. The
-- supplier's QA reads them, which is the half of the story neither
-- organization holds alone.
template IncomingInspection
  with
    producerQa : Party
    producerReceiving : Party
    producerManufacturing : Party
    supplierQa : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    inspectionNumber : Text
    inspectedAt : Time
    tests : [QualityTest]
    conforms : Bool
    remark : Optional Text
  where
    signatory producerQa
    observer producerReceiving, producerManufacturing, supplierQa

    nonconsuming choice ReleaseForProduction : ContractId MaterialRelease
      with
        releaseNumber : Text
        releasedAt : Time
      controller producerQa
      do
        create MaterialRelease with
          producerQa = producerQa
          producerManufacturing = producerManufacturing
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          inspectionNumber = inspectionNumber
          releaseNumber = releaseNumber
          releasedAt = releasedAt

    nonconsuming choice QuarantineLot : ContractId Quarantine
      with
        quarantineNumber : Text
        quarantinedAt : Time
        reason : Text
      controller producerQa
      do
        create Quarantine with
          producerQa = producerQa
          producerReceiving = producerReceiving
          producerManufacturing = producerManufacturing
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          inspectionNumber = inspectionNumber
          quarantineNumber = quarantineNumber
          quarantinedAt = quarantinedAt
          reason = reason

-- | The end of Story 1. Manufacturing may now use the material and the
-- supplier's QA sees that it was released - neither organization holds the
-- whole history alone. `releasedBy` is gone for the reason `receivedBy` is.
template MaterialRelease
  with
    producerQa : Party
    producerManufacturing : Party
    supplierQa : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    inspectionNumber : Text
    releaseNumber : Text
    releasedAt : Time
  where
    signatory producerQa
    observer producerManufacturing, supplierQa
-- | THE PRODUCER'S OWN, AND NOBODY ELSE'S. Story 2's divergence starts here
-- and `fixture_pharma.md` asks for exactly this: "Some information should be
-- visible only to the organization that created or owns it".
--
-- NO SUPPLIER PARTY IS NAMED, which is the whole point. A lot held back is an
-- internal decision until the producer chooses to raise it, and until
-- `RaiseDeviation` the supplier's participant does not know this contract
-- exists. It is the first contract in this fixture that the two organizations
-- do not both see, and it is what makes the Workbench show two different
-- ledgers side by side.
template Quarantine
  with
    producerQa : Party
    producerReceiving : Party
    producerManufacturing : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    inspectionNumber : Text
    quarantineNumber : Text
    quarantinedAt : Time
    reason : Text
  where
    signatory producerQa
    observer producerReceiving, producerManufacturing

    -- | The supplier is named HERE rather than carried on the quarantine,
    -- because a field naming them would put them on the contract and there
    -- would be nothing private about it.
    nonconsuming choice RaiseDeviation : ContractId Deviation
      with
        deviationNumber : Text
        raisedAt : Time
        description : Text
        producerResult : QualityTest
        supplierQa : Party
      controller producerQa
      do
        create Deviation with
          producerQa = producerQa
          producerManufacturing = producerManufacturing
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          quarantineNumber = quarantineNumber
          deviationNumber = deviationNumber
          raisedAt = raisedAt
          description = description
          producerResult = producerResult

    -- | The end of the lot's quarantine, and the one CONSUMING step of Story
    -- 2. The disposition it closes against is named BY CONTRACT ID, so the
    -- archived quarantine points at what resolved it rather than repeating it.
    choice CloseQuarantine : ()
      with
        closedAt : Time
        disposition : ContractId Disposition
      controller producerQa
      do
        return ()

-- | Raised TO the supplier: the producer's disagreement, with the measurement
-- under it. Signed by the producer alone - an assertion the supplier cannot
-- alter - and observed by the supplier's Quality Assurance, who answers it.
template Deviation
  with
    producerQa : Party
    producerManufacturing : Party
    supplierQa : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    quarantineNumber : Text
    deviationNumber : Text
    raisedAt : Time
    description : Text
    producerResult : QualityTest
  where
    signatory producerQa
    observer producerManufacturing, supplierQa

    nonconsuming choice Respond : ContractId SupplierResponse
      with
        respondedAt : Time
        note : Text
        evidence : ResponseEvidence
      controller supplierQa
      do
        create SupplierResponse with
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          producerQa = producerQa
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          deviationNumber = deviationNumber
          respondedAt = respondedAt
          note = note
          evidence = evidence

-- | The supplier's answer, signed by the supplier - which is the half of the
-- history the producer cannot write.
--
-- A NOTE AND A VARIANT, where there were three loose fields. Two Optionals
-- beside a Text said a supplier might answer with both, neither or either, and
-- what `fixture_pharma.md` describes is ONE answer of a known kind. The note
-- is the covering sentence and is always there; `evidence` is what was
-- actually offered.
template SupplierResponse
  with
    supplierQa : Party
    producerQa : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    deviationNumber : Text
    respondedAt : Time
    note : Text
    evidence : ResponseEvidence
  where
    signatory supplierQa
    observer producerQa

    nonconsuming choice OrderRetest : ContractId Retest
      with
        retestNumber : Text
        retestedAt : Time
        tests : [QualityTest]
        conforms : Bool
        conditions : TextMap Text
      controller producerQa
      do
        create Retest with
          producerQa = producerQa
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          deviationNumber = deviationNumber
          retestNumber = retestNumber
          retestedAt = retestedAt
          tests = tests
          conforms = conforms
          conditions = conditions

-- | The producer testing again, with the supplier's answer in hand. Its
-- results are what the disposition is taken against.
--
-- `conditions` IS A MAP, and it is here because a retest is the one record in
-- the fixture whose circumstances matter as much as its numbers - which
-- instrument, which operator, which method. MEASURED 2026-09-22: a `TextMap`
-- goes as a JSON OBJECT and an array of pairs is refused with `Expected
-- ujson.Obj`.
template Retest
  with
    producerQa : Party
    supplierQa : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    deviationNumber : Text
    retestNumber : Text
    retestedAt : Time
    tests : [QualityTest]
    conforms : Bool
    conditions : TextMap Text
  where
    signatory producerQa
    observer supplierQa

    -- | Manufacturing is a CHOICE ARGUMENT rather than a field of this
    -- contract: the retest is a quality record and has no reason to name the
    -- people who will or will not receive the material.
    nonconsuming choice Dispose : ContractId Disposition
      with
        dispositionNumber : Text
        decidedAt : Time
        outcome : DispositionOutcome
        rationale : Text
        producerManufacturing : Party
      controller producerQa
      do
        create Disposition with
          producerQa = producerQa
          producerManufacturing = producerManufacturing
          supplierQa = supplierQa
          lotNumber = lotNumber
          deviationNumber = deviationNumber
          dispositionNumber = dispositionNumber
          decidedAt = decidedAt
          outcome = outcome
          rationale = rationale

-- | How Story 2 ends. The producer decides and the supplier reads it, which
-- is the shape every quality decision in this fixture has.
--
-- `outcome` IS THE ENUM now - 2026-09-22, once `types_probe.py` had measured
-- what one looks like inbound. It was Text carrying one of the five names,
-- which is a comment where a type belongs.
template Disposition
  with
    producerQa : Party
    producerManufacturing : Party
    supplierQa : Party
    lotNumber : Text
    deviationNumber : Text
    dispositionNumber : Text
    decidedAt : Time
    outcome : DispositionOutcome
    rationale : Text
  where
    signatory producerQa
    observer producerManufacturing, supplierQa
